              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:poverty_group:nk]>]]></run>
              <run> of the 37 states, by MPI&#10;Of the population, </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:headcount_ratio_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>% are multidimensionally poor&#10;</run>
              <run>Average deprivation among them: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:intensity_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>% of the things counted&#10;</run>
              <run>Poor people: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_poor_thousands:qk]>]]></run>
              <run> thousand&#10;</run>
              <run>Made up of: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:dim_hover:nk]>]]></run>
              <run>&#10;</run>
              <run>Governorship 1999&#8211;2021: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:gov_party:nk]>]]></run>
              <run bold='true'>&#10;&#10;MPI </run>
              <run bold='true'><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run bold='true'>%</run>
              <run>  (95% interval </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_ci_lo_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>% to </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_ci_hi_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>%)&#10;</run>
              <run italic='true'>MPI is the share of people who are poor multiplied by how deprived they are, as a percentage of the index.&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run italic='true'>Neighbouring states' intervals overlap, so the map groups states into bands instead of ranking them.</run>
            </formatted-text>
          </customized-tooltip>
